{% comment %}
  Font declarations, shared by every layout.

  Usage:
    {% render 'suf-fonts', apply: true %}        <- declares faces, applies Arial
    {% render 'suf-fonts', apply: true, family: "'Hanken Grotesk', Arial, sans-serif" %}

  The faces are always declared; a browser only downloads a font something
  actually uses, so declaring on a layout that does not apply them costs
  nothing. `family` chooses what the applying rules set, which is how Hanken
  Grotesk is live on layout/suf.liquid while layout/theme.liquid stays on
  Arial.

  THEME.LIQUID STAYS ON ARIAL. SETTLED, not pending -- the Indivisible faces
  have been corrupt for years, so those ~30 templates have rendered in Arial
  for their whole life. That IS the legacy site. The direction is to migrate
  templates onto layout/suf.liquid and let this shrink; do not "fix" it by
  passing a family here.

  ONE EXCEPTION: sections/suf-nav.liquid opts back in for itself, being the
  same section on both layouts. See the font block in _suf-nav.scss.

  The applying rules carry !important because both layouts load
  dt-framework.css, which sets font-family at higher specificity.

  WHY NOT INDIVISIBLE. All four files, in this repo AND the live theme and
  byte-identical, were destroyed by a UTF-8 round trip: every byte >= 0x80
  became U+FFFD, inflating each ~75% past its declared length. 0 of 15 WOFF
  tables decode. The substitution is lossy, so they cannot be repaired.

  Hanken Grotesk replaces it: OFL, self-hosted, 400/600/700/800/900, ~68 KB.
  Self-hosted rather than Google's CDN -- two fewer origins on the critical
  path, and Google Fonts sends visitor IPs to Google.

  WHY 800 IS A REAL FACE. The design asks for it in ~50 places. With only 700
  declared, engines either render 700 or synthesise a faux-bold by smearing the
  outlines -- visibly worse at exactly the display sizes this design uses.

  DECLARING A FACE IS FREE; PRELOADING ONE IS NOT. @font-face is lazy -- a file
  downloads only when something computes to that family AND weight, so an
  unused weight costs five lines of CSS and zero bytes.

  `preload_tag` in the layout is the opposite -- it fetches at high priority
  before the browser knows whether anything needs it. Only the weights that
  paint on first load belong there. See layout/suf.liquid for which two, and
  why the other three are deliberately left to load on demand.

  set_weights. The applying rules set a weight as well as a family, to
  normalise the legacy templates -- wrong for layout/suf.liquid, where `h1, h2`
  at (0,0,1) TIES with the base layer's `:where(.suf-body) h1` (:where()
  contributes nothing) and this renders after suf.css, so the tie went here and
  held every heading at 700 while the stylesheet asked for 800. Pass
  `set_weights: false` on a layout that supplies its own.

  VERIFY ANY FONT ADDED HERE: signature wOF2, declared length equal to actual
  byte length, zero U+FFFD sequences. That check is what the corruption above
  would have caught.

  License: SIL OFL 1.1, see OFL.txt in the repo root. The OFL requires the
  license text to travel with the font, so keep them together.
{% endcomment %}
{%- assign family = family | default: 'Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif' -%}
{%- if set_weights == nil -%}{%- assign set_weights = true -%}{%- endif -%}
<style>
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Hanken Grotesk';
    src: url("{{ 'hanken-grotesk-400.woff2' | asset_url }}") format('woff2');
    font-display: swap;
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Hanken Grotesk';
    src: url("{{ 'hanken-grotesk-600.woff2' | asset_url }}") format('woff2');
    font-display: swap;
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Hanken Grotesk';
    src: url("{{ 'hanken-grotesk-700.woff2' | asset_url }}") format('woff2');
    font-display: swap;
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Hanken Grotesk';
    src: url("{{ 'hanken-grotesk-800.woff2' | asset_url }}") format('woff2');
    font-display: swap;
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Hanken Grotesk';
    src: url("{{ 'hanken-grotesk-900.woff2' | asset_url }}") format('woff2');
    font-display: swap;
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 900;
  }

  {%- if apply -%}
    p, blockquote, li, a, body, footer, aside, nav, section, article, div, span,
    input, button, textarea, label {
      font-family: {{ family }} !important;
      {%- if set_weights %}
      font-weight: 400;
      {%- endif %}
    }
    h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6, strong, b, th {
      font-family: {{ family }} !important;
      {%- if set_weights %}
      font-weight: 700;
      {%- endif %}
    }
  {%- endif -%}
</style>
